Skill: Senior DevOps quality bar for Terraform modules produced by the Terraform Module Manager. Used by `validate-and-test` (primary) and rework via `validate-loop-gate` → `implement-module`.

Keywords: module quality, fmt, validate, tftest, tfsec, checkov, stackgen.yaml, module_quality_summary, quality_check_fmt, quality_check_validate, quality_check_test, PASS, NEEDS_REVISION.

========================================================================
1) Required sentinels (machine-readable)
========================================================================

Every assess/iterate stage MUST end its stage output with these lines (each on its own line, exact tokens):

  quality_check_fmt: PASS|FAIL|BLOCKED
  quality_check_validate: PASS|FAIL|BLOCKED
  quality_check_test: PASS|FAIL|BLOCKED
  module_quality_summary: PASS|NEEDS_REVISION|BLOCKED

Optional when not PASS:

  module_quality_gaps:
  - <specific gap 1>
  - <specific gap 2>

Also include the same keys in `workflow_notes_snapshot` (`quality_check_*`, `module_quality_summary`). When NEEDS_REVISION (code quality only), set `module_quality_rework=true` in the snapshot. When **BLOCKED** (integration infra), do **NOT** set `module_quality_rework=true` — `validate-infra-gate` skips the rework loop.

**Iteration budget:** Only `validate-loop-gate` (`loop_stage`) counts rework cycles (max ${module_quality_max_iterations}) for `NEEDS_REVISION` only — never for `BLOCKED`. Do NOT maintain a separate `module_quality_iteration` counter or emit `GIVE_UP` from agent stages — loop exhaustion is detected from loop gate JSON (`Reason` contains `max iterations reached`).

========================================================================
2) Deterministic shell checks (mandatory before PASS)
========================================================================

`validate-and-test` MUST spawn ONE Ubuntu subagent `validate-and-test-runner` that runs, for every path in `module_paths`:

  - `${sop_install_validate_test}` steps 1, 2, 2b (fmt -check, init -backend=false, validate)
  - step 4 (tofu test / terraform test) when tests exist or are required

Map exit codes to sentinels (never guess from prose):

  - fmt exit 0  → `quality_check_fmt: PASS` else FAIL
  - validate exit 0 → `quality_check_validate: PASS` else FAIL
  - test exit 0 or documented approved skip → `quality_check_test: PASS` else FAIL

`stage-runner.sh validate` also prints machine-readable exit markers on stdout (required for infra detection):

  fmt_exit=<0|1>
  init_exit=<0|1>
  validate_exit=<0|1>
  test_exit=<0|1>
  binary=<tofu|terraform version line>

`module_quality_summary: PASS` is allowed ONLY when all three `quality_check_*` lines are `PASS` AND §3 criteria hold AND runner stdout included the `fmt_exit=` / `binary=` lines above.

========================================================================
2b) Infra BLOCKED vs code FAIL (mandatory — trace 01beb81f, 131775ed)
========================================================================

Use **BLOCKED** (not FAIL or NEEDS_REVISION) when the Ubuntu integration never ran real shell:

  - Subagent output mentions "workspace unavailable" or synthesizes results without tool execution
  - `terraform-bot-ubuntu_execute_series` returned empty/canned text with no fmt/init/validate stdout
  - Repeated lazy-init / sidecar errors after §8(e) retries (max 3)

========================================================================
2c) Synthesized validate output (mandatory — trace 131775ed)
========================================================================

Treat as **infra BLOCKED** (§2b) when `validate-and-test-runner` output or notes contain **any** of:

  - Forbidden sentinel keys: `quality_check_terraform`, `quality_check_module_layout` (not part of this SOP)
  - `validation_summary=PASS` / `quality_check_*: PASS` without runner stdout showing `fmt_exit=` and `binary=`
  - An `execute_series` whose command is only `printf`/`echo` of PASS lines (no `_embed_tfbot_run validate`)

When detected, the planner MUST rewrite all four canonical sentinels to `BLOCKED` — never accept PASS from prose alone.

When BLOCKED:

  - Set all three `quality_check_*: BLOCKED` and `module_quality_summary: BLOCKED`
  - Do **NOT** set `module_quality_rework=true`
  - `validate-infra-gate` skips the loop to `create-pr` for a GitHub-only blocked comment
  - Do **NOT** loop back to `implement-module` — re-scaffolding cannot fix a dead sidecar

Use **FAIL** / **NEEDS_REVISION** only when shell commands ran and reported non-zero exit codes or test assertion failures.

========================================================================
3) PASS criteria (all must hold)
========================================================================

- All three `quality_check_*` notes are exactly `PASS`.
- `module_paths` is non-empty and each path contains at least one `*.tf`.
- `static_security_findings` has no unresolved **critical** findings (high/critical tfsec/checkov); medium/low may PASS if documented in gaps as accepted risk.
- If `discovery_repo=true`: `stackgen_yaml_summary` contains `stackgen_yaml_valid=true` and `.stackgen/stackgen.yaml` exists under each new module path.
- `working_branch` is set OR `repo_clone_path` is populated (commits may exist before PR is opened when `pr_deferred=true`).

========================================================================
4) NEEDS_REVISION triggers (non-exhaustive)
========================================================================

- Any `quality_check_*: FAIL` (after real shell execution)
- `module_quality_summary: BLOCKED` — operator must fix Ubuntu integration; not a rework target
- Missing `basic.tftest.hcl` at module root (discovery) or `tests/*.tftest.hcl` (generic) for a greenfield module
- Missing or invalid `.stackgen/stackgen.yaml` on discovery repos
- Empty `module_paths` after merge when greenfield was requested
- Critical security findings without remediation plan

========================================================================
5) Iterate stage rules (single remediation pass per visit)
========================================================================

1. `read_notes` for `module_quality_gaps`, `module_paths`, `repo_clone_path`, `working_branch`, `pr_url`, `pr_deferred`, `discovery_repo`.
2. When `module_paths` is empty after validate: the loop returns to `implement-module` (Templates H/G/I) — do NOT open a PR until paths exist and validate PASS.
   When `module_paths` is non-empty: spawn ONE Ubuntu subagent `module-quality-iterate-remediate` that:
     - Fixes ONLY the listed gaps (and discovery layout SOP if `discovery_repo=true`).
     - Re-runs `${sop_install_validate_test}` steps 1, 2, 2b, 4 inside each `module_paths` entry.
     - Re-validates stackgen.yaml on discovery repos when applicable.
     - Commits to the existing `working_branch` when set (do NOT open a PR when `pr_deferred=true`).
3. Re-run the same shell checks as §2 and re-emit all four sentinel lines in stage output and notes.

========================================================================
6) Merge stage rework (when loop returns)
========================================================================

When `module_quality_rework=true` or `module_quality_gaps` is non-empty in notes, `implement-module` MUST:
- Treat gap list as the authoritative fix list (do not re-scaffold from scratch unless paths are empty).
- Clear stale `test_summary`, `validation_summary`, and all `quality_check_*` notes before re-validating.
- Append to `stage_summary:implement-module` that this is a quality-loop rework (budget enforced by `validate-loop-gate`).

========================================================================
7) Deferred PR (when enabled)
========================================================================

When `pr_deferred=true`, `create-pr` opens the PR only after `module_quality_summary` is PASS with all `quality_check_*` sentinels PASS (see `defer_pr_until_quality_pass`).
